A||||1||BN Boomer||More greenhorn questions
Z||000000||BN Boomer||08-05-99||03:23 PM||||Okay guys, what is the wire bundle that enters the rear deck lid on the passenger's side for? Looks like 2 or 3 wires. Is it for a remote lock release? My 87 SC doesn't have the switch on the dash. Is the wiring for it in place on all Fiero's and is it an easy retrofit?<p>Also, I notice a gasoline odor when sitting in the car with the ignition on, engine not running. I suspect a small leak in the fuel lines somewhere. Anyone else had this problem?
Z||000001||theogre||08-05-99||03:42 PM||||A gas leak is a good bet.<p>The wire bundle is for the ajar switch. The 3 wire harness has to be replaced to add the trunk latch. there is a paper about adding the trunk latch option.<p> <A HREF="http://home.sprynet.com/~theogre/fiero/pfindex.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://home.sprynet.com/~theogre/fiero/pfindex.htm</A> 
